@startuml t10-mcp-lifecycle
title MCP Lifecycle: Streamable HTTP (2025-06-18)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

participant "MCP Client" as client #aliceblue
participant "MCP Server" as server #palegreen

== Initialization ==
client -> server : POST initialize (id: 1)\nVersion, client capabilities, client info
server --> client : Initialize result (id: 1)\nVersion, server capabilities, server info
note over client, server #lightyellow
  The server may assign an Mcp-Session-Id.
  Subsequent requests include the negotiated
  MCP-Protocol-Version and any assigned session ID.
end note
client ->> server : POST notifications/initialized (no id)
server --> client : HTTP 202 Accepted (no body)

== Operation: Discovery and Action ==
client -> server : POST tools/list (id: 2)
server --> client : Tool names, descriptions, input schemas
client -> server : POST tools/call (id: 5)\nget_user_by_id(user_id: 999)
server --> client : Tool result or JSON-RPC error (id: 5)
note over client, server #lightcyan
  Resources: resources/list, then resources/read.
  Prompts: prompts/list, then prompts/get.
  Request responses may use JSON or SSE.
end note

== Shutdown ==
opt Session assigned and no longer needed
  client -> server : DELETE MCP endpoint + session/version headers
  server --> client : Terminated, or HTTP 405 if unsupported
end
note over client, server #lightyellow
  Close associated HTTP connections and SSE streams.
  MCP has no JSON-RPC shutdown method.
end note
@enduml